{%- doc -%}
The header's cart icon: the theme's bag and, stacked on top of it, a happy face. When a product is added to the cart the bag turns into the face for a
moment and back (CSS and script in sections/header.liquid, .header__cart-icon). While the cart has items (.has-items) the bag is filled solid with the
icon's own color. Both icons take the same size and stroke width.

@param {number} [width] - the icon width on desktop
@param {number} [mobile_width] - the icon width on mobile

With the "Shopping cart" icon (theme settings > cart icon) the number of items is shown inside its basket (.header__cart-icon-count).
{%- enddoc -%}

<span class="header__cart-icon{% unless cart.empty? %} has-items{% endunless %}"{% if settings.cart_icon == 'shopping_cart' %} style="--cart-icon-width: {{ width | default: 16 }}px; --cart-icon-mobile-width: {{ mobile_width | default: width | default: 16 }}px"{% endif %}>
  {%- render 'icon' with 'cart', mobile_width: mobile_width, width: width, class: 'header__cart-icon-bag' -%}
  {%- render 'icon' with 'cart-smile', mobile_width: mobile_width, width: width, class: 'header__cart-icon-smile' -%}
  {%- if settings.cart_icon == 'shopping_cart' -%}
    {%- comment -%}The number of items, inside the basket of the shopping cart icon; <cart-count> keeps it up to date (and hides it when the cart is empty){%- endcomment -%}
    <cart-count class="header__cart-icon-count"{% if cart.empty? %} hidden{% endif %}><span>{{ cart.item_count }}</span></cart-count>
  {%- endif -%}
</span>
